Build the reading half of design §4.4 *A filing PR nobody holds is a work order*, the bullet *A filing PR*:
- `workorders.filing_paths(root)`: the ledger's paths (`ledger.ledger_path`: a v2 directory, its `archive/` included; or a v1 ledger's file and its `ledger.archive_path`), the board (`workorders.board_rel`) and the board's archive (`workorders.archive_rel`).
- `reports.filing(files, paths) -> bool`: true when every changed file is one of `paths` or under a directory among them; false for an empty list. `reports` never imports `workorders`.
- `pr_reading` takes `filing=` (the paths) beside `held=`; the tick passes `workorders.filing_paths(root)` as it passes the held key. In the held read (`reports._held_flags`): stamp `filing` and `filing_head` on every open non-sync PR, once per head, carried from `olds` as `held` is, read again for a changed head, whatever the held key (an empty key reads files for `filing` alone and leaves `held` as today). One `pr_files` call serves both when both are due; the reads share `HELD_READS`, due rows oldest first by `created` as today; a failed read keeps the last word; a PR never read carries no `filing`.
